\f1 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Looking at Ezekiel 24:1-14 in Hebrew after chapters 22-23, I see three intensifications that demand attention:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0

\b \cf2 The date and the siege (vv. 1-2):
\b0 \
The siege begins 
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1456 \u1468 \u1506 \u1462 \u1510 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1497 \u1468 \u1493 \u1465 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1494 \u1462 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  - "this very day" (twice). The emphasis on exact timing matters. Unlike prophecies that can be deflected as "for distant times" (12:27), this one is marked, dated, undeniable. When it happens, the correspondence will be perfect.\

\b The pot's corruption (vv. 3-6):
\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <notes> Need to trace the pot metaphor from chapter 11 carefully and show how it inverts. Also need to connect chelah (corruption/rust) to the broader theme of structural versus removable impurity. </notes>\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Chapter 11:3 had Jerusalem's inhabitants claiming: "this city is the pot, and we are the meat" - asserting protection, preservation. But verse 6 here: 
\f2 \uc0\u1505 \u1460 \u1497 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1458 \u1513 \u1462 \u1473 \u1512 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1462 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1514 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1495 \u1462 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1514 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1465 \u1488 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1497 \u1464 \u1510 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1502 \u1460 \u1502 \u1462 \u1468 \u1504 \u1464 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  - "a pot whose corrosion/rust is in it, and whose corrosion has not gone out from it."\
The word 
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1462 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  (chelah) appears repeatedly (vv. 6, 11, 12 twice, 13). This isn't removable dirt. It's rust, structural corruption of the bronze itself. The container meant to preserve has become contaminated at a level that ordinary cleaning cannot reach.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0

\b \cf2 The exposed blood (v. 7):
\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0

