"For her blood was in the midst of her; she set it on the bare rock; she did not pour it on the ground to cover it with dust."\
Leviticus 17:13 requires covering blood with earth. Genesis 4:10 shows Abel's blood crying from the ground. But Jerusalem placed her bloodshed 
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1463 \u1500 \u1470 \u1510 \u1456 \u1495 \u1460 \u1497 \u1495 \u1463 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1505 \u1462 \u1500 \u1463 \u1506 
\f1  - "on bare rock" - exposed, public, unashamed. This connects directly to chapter 22's accusation: bloodshed encompassing economic exploitation, oppression of the vulnerable, all forms of predation (22:6-12). That blood was never covered because those committing it saw no need for covering.\
Verse 8 reveals the purpose: 
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1456 \u1492 \u1463 \u1506 \u1458 \u1500 \u1493 \u1465 \u1514 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1461 \u1502 \u1464 \u1492 
