\f1  - "To rouse fury, to take vengeance, I have set her blood on the bare rock, that it may not be covered." YHWH Himself ensures the blood remains exposed - guaranteeing that it cries out, that vengeance comes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0

\b \cf2 The failed purification (vv. 11-13):
\b0 \
The empty pot placed on coals (v. 11) attempts purification through extreme heat. But verse 12: 
\f2 \uc0\u1514 \u1456 \u1468 \u1488 \u1467 \u1504 \u1460 \u1497 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1462 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1514 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1500 \u1465 \u1488 \u1470 \u1514 \u1461 \u1510 \u1461 \u1488 
