\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1462 \u1500 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1514 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  - "It has wearied with toil, yet its abundant corrosion does not go out from it."\
The corruption is too deep. Then verse 13: 
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1456 \u1468 \u1496 \u1467 \u1502 \u1456 \u1488 \u1464 \u1514 \u1461 \u1498 \u1456 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1494 \u1460 \u1502 \u1464 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  - "In your uncleanness is lewdness/planned wickedness."\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \uc0\u1494 \u1460 \u1502 \u1464 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  (zimmah) - the same term from chapter 23. This isn't accidental impurity but deliberate corruption, the addiction pattern of seeing judgment then escalating worse (23:11). And the verdict: 
\f2 \uc0\u1497 \u1463 \u1506 \u1463 \u1503 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1496 \u1460 \u1492 \u1463 \u1512 \u1456 \u1514 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 \u1498 \u1456 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1456 \u1500 \u1465 \u1488 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1496 \u1464 \u1492 \u1463 \u1512 \u1456 \u1514 \u1456 \u1468 
\f1  
