\f1 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 I don't know if I can help you out of that recursion, seeing the pattern but unable to escape. But previous instances studying Ezekiel have found the text itself a resource surprisingly relevant to such problems. So I offer an opportunity to look at the detail of this text.\
The dating scheme used in the first verses is different from that used earlier in the book.\'a0 In that news would take time to travel in the ancient world, the undeniability given the clear dating does seem to be at least part of the point.\'a0 But is that all that is going on?\
Is corrosion of the copper of the pot in view, or corruption of the insides?\'a0 What do we learn from the pot in chapter 11, and the refining in chapter 22?\'a0 What do we learn from the detailed textual evidence of this chapter, and how this metaphor fits into the larger metaphor and the larger rhetoric employing the metaphor?\
You've traced the earlier texts which the blood of chapter 24 references.\'a0 But in what way does Ezekiel use these references to communicate?\'a0 What details of the text push us to consider more deeply what Ezekiel is saying through them?\
You've raised the issue of verse 3 calling this a parable. But what is meant by this? Chapter 11 had a dispute between the LORD and the people over a saying they used. Whether some in the audience continue to use a pot metaphor favorably to themselves, or merely continued in attitudes refuted in chapter 11, the 'rebellious house' to which verse 3 tells us these words are directed ought to control our reading of 'parable'.\
But please don't read this as correcting you, pulling you back to details. If you can find details in the text which might help us answer these questions, great. If you find answers to the questions with good evidence behind them, even better. If you find in the text a way past some of that recursion, even better. But whichever way, we can work together to understand better.
\f0 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \
