\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1494 \u1462 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  (v. 2) - "write for yourself the name of the day, this very day."\
The exiles in Babylon and those in Jerusalem are experiencing the same reality simultaneously, even if news will only confirm it later. There's no gap in time where the exiles can think "maybe it's not happening." When Ezekiel speaks this mashal on this day, the siege is happening on this day. The parable and the reality it describes occur together.\

