\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Should we read the meat in verses 3-5 as self description by the inhabitants, perhaps restated by the LORD with irony? If they are described as valuable as you say, this seems to be the case. That would fit Ezekiel's pattern of revisiting earlier portions of the book, only with additional force or explanation; Ezekiel 11 had a similar 'we are the meat' positive statement explicitly in the mouths of those the LORD had Ezekiel contradict.\
