The opening isn't just resumption of prophecy - it's the removal of the constraint against intercession. For the first time since his call, Ezekiel will be able to plead with his people from his own heart, to intercede for them with YHWH. The iron wall comes down. The silenced tongue is freed.\
The hope is that after judgment is complete and recognized, intercession becomes possible again. There's Someone to intercede to, Someone who will hear, because the fury has been satisfied (v. 13's 
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1463 \u1491 
\f1 ).\
