\b \cf2 The ending with not mourning:
\b0 \
This is profound. Chapters 1-24 build through escalating judgment declarations - bloodshed, false prophets, harlotry, the pot, the sword. The expected endpoint would be mourning: proper grief, lament, ritual processing of catastrophic loss.\
But instead: 
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1468 \u1504 \u1456 \u1502 \u1463 \u1511 \u1465 \u1468 \u1514 \u1462 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1463 \u1468 \u1506 \u1458 \u1493 
\f3 \uc0\u1466 \'f0\'c9\'fa\'c5\'e9\'eb\'c6\'ed
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1493 \u1468 \u1504 \u1456 \u1492 \u1463 \u1502 \u1456 \u1514 \u1462 \u1468 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1460 \u1497 \u1513 \u1473 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1488 \u1462 \u1500 \u1470 \u1488 \u1464 \u1495 \u1460 \u1497 \u1493 
\f1  (v. 23) - "you shall waste away in your iniquities and groan, each to his brother."\
Mourning is how you move through loss toward acceptance or resolution. The prohibition on mourning means no resolution, no closure, no moving past it. Instead: ongoing recognition. Wasting away is continuous, not a process that completes.\
The section ends with unresolved grief, with groaning to one another, with wasting away that continues 
\f2 \uc0\u1506 \u1463 \u1491 
\f1  - until (v. 13). Not mourning means staying in the recognition, not processing through it.\
But then verse 27 breaks this: 
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1463 \u1468 \u1497 \u1468 \u1493 \u1465 \u1501 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1492 \u1463 \u1492 \u1493 \u1468 \u1488 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1497 \u1460 \u1508 \u1464 \u1468 \u1514 \u1463 \u1495 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1508 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 \u1498 \u1464 
\f1  - "In that day your mouth will be opened." The resolution doesn't come through human mourning ritual but through divine action - the opening of the prophet's mouth, the restoration of intercession possibility, the knowledge that I am YHWH.\
The ending with not mourning means: human processes cannot resolve what divine judgment has done. You cannot mourn your way through deserved judgment into acceptance. You can only waste away in recognition until YHWH acts to open what was closed - the mouth, the possibility of intercession, the pathway forward.\
The 24 chapters end not with closure but with enforced openness to what comes next. The grief cannot be processed and set aside. It must remain until the mouth opens, until they know I am YHWH, until whatever YHWH does next with a people who have finally, through wasting away, recognized their iniquities.
