\b The rebellious house's error:
\b0 \
They didn't take His word seriously - neither the warnings nor the promises. Either they presumed the temple guaranteed protection (ignoring the curses, thinking covenant meant immunity), or they would later despair that judgment meant total abandonment (ignoring the restoration promises, thinking curses meant rejection).\
Both errors stem from not believing YHWH means what He says. The judgment declares: I meant the warnings. The structure leading to opened mouth and recognition declares: I also mean the promises.\

